----------------------------------------------------------------------
fork changes (multithreaded server, fps-friendly, skills, wasd)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

threads
- net thread (epoll/select) -> handlers under the world lock.
- tick thread at 10Hz (CFG_TICK_MS, was 1 second).
- sender pool: each connection has an outbox, packets produced in a tick
  are flushed together and written to the socket outside the world lock,
  so a slow client never stalls the rest.
- job pool: visibility (who sees what) is computed for all players in
  parallel.
- threads stop cleanly before a hot reload and start again after it.

why the client fps improves (the c4 client itself can't be changed)
- interest management: a client only hears about objects within
  CFG_VIEW_ENTER (3000) and never more than CFG_MAX_KNOWN (120, nearest
  first, sticky). the original sent everything to everybody in the world.
- no more ValidateLocation spam to moving players (the check was inverted).
- keyboard moves from other players are throttled (CFG_KEYBOARD_BCAST_MS).
- packets are batched per tick, TCP_NODELAY on.

skills (gs_combat.c, data driven)
- daggers (rogue/treasure hunter/scout/plains walker/assassin/abyss
  walker...): Mortal Blow, Backstab (from behind only), Deadly Blow and
  Shadow Step (821): teleports you behind the target, which can't turn
  around nor attack for 1.2s. blows always land from behind.
- dwarves: Power Strike, Stun Attack, Hammer Crush (stun), Wild Sweep
  (area), Fatal Strike, Battle Roar; +20% hp, +18% p.atk, +12% p.def.
- stats per race/class (the stored ones were placeholders: speed 20...).

wasd / keyboard movement
- server: echo to the mover immediately, throttle for observers, clamp the
  lead point, trust the client within CFG_DESYNC_TOLERANCE (no rubber
  band), correct beyond it (no speed/teleport hacks), detect key release.
- client/ue5/L2KeyboardMover.h: prediction + minimal packets + blended
  corrections for a custom ue5 client (example component included).

fixes
- crash (segfault in wqueue) with ~40 players; request buffer overflow;
  packet size 0 infinite loop; u32 distance overflow; null character
  dereference on early packets; path traversal through character names;
  socket leak on linux; windows select limited to 64 sockets.

tests (linux): bash tests/run_all.sh [tsan|asan]
- smoke, wasd, mover (c++ mover vs server), fuzz, load, siege.

not validated yet against a real c4 client: Shadow Step visuals (it's an
interlude skill), the c4 MagicSkillUse/SkillList trailing bytes, and
CharInfo for players (CFG_SEND_PLAYER_CHARINFO, off by default).
the windows build was not compiled here (no msvc), only linux.
